== B.1 The Subject and its Tools (Questions 1–15)

#mcq(1, [Which pair of words best completes the definition: geography studies the \_\_\_\_ distribution of phenomena and the \_\_\_\_ between people and environment?],
  [random; separation],
  [chemical; reaction],
  [spatial; relationship],
  [historical; conflict]
)

#mcq(2, [A candidate who explains why markets cluster at road junctions is working in],
  [meteorology],
  [human geography],
  [physical geography],
  [cartography]
)

#mcq(3, [The four spheres of the earth system are the lithosphere, atmosphere, hydrosphere and],
  [ozone layer],
  [biosphere],
  [mesosphere],
  [stratosphere]
)

#mcq(4, [Which tool would best show how land use has changed over twenty years?],
  [a series of satellite images],
  [a questionnaire],
  [a rain gauge],
  [a single photograph]
)

#mcq(5, [A map differs from a photograph chiefly because a map],
  [is always in colour],
  [selects and represents features with symbols to scale],
  [shows only relief],
  [cannot be revised]
)

#mcq(6, [The geographer's interest in a mineral deposit is mainly in its],
  [melting point],
  [location and the consequences of that location],
  [crystal structure],
  [chemical formula]
)

#mcq(7, [Weather differs from climate in that weather is],
  [a type of rainfall],
  [the average over thirty years],
  [the state of the atmosphere at a moment],
  [a description of ocean currents]
)

#mcq(8, [Which of these best describes a sketch map?],
  [a map with a stated scale and grid],
  [a cross-section],
  [a satellite image],
  [a simplified drawing showing relative positions]
)

#mcq(9, [The study of soils as a geographical topic belongs most directly to],
  [physical geography],
  [cartography],
  [human geography],
  [statistics]
)

#mcq(10, [Remote sensing is most useful to a geographer because it],
  [provides repeated images of large areas],
  [measures rainfall directly],
  [draws maps automatically],
  [replaces fieldwork entirely]
